1
00:00:01,635 --> 00:00:03,270
REMEMBER

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:05,572
IT'S BETTER TO BURN OUT

3
00:00:05,639 --> 00:00:10,377
IN A SINGLE MOMENT
THAN TO FADE AWAY.

4
00:00:10,444 --> 00:00:12,279
KURT COBAIN

5
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,249
Let's roll!

6
00:00:17,451 --> 00:00:18,752
Let's go!

7
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:21,421
Go, go, go!

8
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:23,657
Make way!

9
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,569
EPISODE 1

10
00:00:35,636 --> 00:00:37,638
Hey, steer it straight!

11
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,509
Steer it straight!

12
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:44,678
Hey, watch where you're going!

13
00:00:46,813 --> 00:00:48,682
Wait, hold up! Stop!

14
00:00:48,749 --> 00:00:50,651
I'm getting a call.

15
00:00:50,717 --> 00:00:51,919
Hello?

16
00:00:51,985 --> 00:00:54,588
Quit yelling! We're almost there!

17
00:00:54,655 --> 00:00:57,124
Why'd you guzzle
soju again? Why?

18
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:59,660
The crowd's about to explode,
you punks!

19
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:02,796
Get here now, you bastards!

20
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:04,898
Okay, just five more minutes.

21
00:01:04,965 --> 00:01:06,767
Just five minutes. Hey, stop!

22
00:01:07,868 --> 00:01:09,970
Cheol, we need to step on the gas.

23
00:01:10,037 --> 00:01:12,739
-What gas pedal, you punk?
-It's right there. Step on it!

24
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,776
-Step on the gas!
-I'm exhausted.

25
00:01:15,842 --> 00:01:17,945
Step on the gas! Hurry, get up!

26
00:01:18,011 --> 00:01:20,147
-Hurry, hurry!
-I'm seriously wiped out.

27
00:01:20,213 --> 00:01:21,081
Gi-jun!

28
00:01:21,148 --> 00:01:22,716
-That's it!
-I'm really running!

29
00:01:22,783 --> 00:01:24,284
Hit the booster! Yeah! Go!

30
00:01:24,351 --> 00:01:25,586
WHY SO SERIOUS?

31
00:01:28,455 --> 00:01:29,856
Go, go!

32
00:01:37,064 --> 00:01:39,266
Out of the way, everyone!

33
00:01:40,901 --> 00:01:44,404
Love like a child when you're in love

34
00:01:45,205 --> 00:01:48,709
I think I'm in love right now

35
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:51,278
Love honestly when you're in love

36
00:01:51,345 --> 00:01:52,913
Wait, stop! What is that?

37
00:01:55,482 --> 00:01:58,385
Even if I give you my all

38
00:01:58,452 --> 00:02:00,887
And still feel happy

39
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:04,891
I must be in love with you now

40
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,961
Will you hear my heart?

41
00:02:08,028 --> 00:02:12,299
Shall I send it on the wind?

42
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:15,636
Will my heart show again?

43
00:02:15,702 --> 00:02:19,272
Shall I secretlylong for you?

44
00:02:21,108 --> 00:02:24,044
Filling the whole world

45
00:02:32,252 --> 00:02:34,287
Thank goodness, he's moving!

46
00:02:37,624 --> 00:02:40,027
-Min-gi!
-You scared me half to death!

47
00:02:40,093 --> 00:02:41,662
-Rock and roll!
-Yeah!

48
00:02:44,231 --> 00:02:46,233
-Quit drinking already.
-Awesome!

49
00:02:48,969 --> 00:02:50,504
Are you okay?

50
00:02:51,705 --> 00:02:53,006
Honey!

51
00:02:56,576 --> 00:02:58,478
-What the heck?
-Look, a muscleman.

52
00:02:58,545 --> 00:03:00,380
Hey, get over here.

53
00:03:00,447 --> 00:03:02,449
Get over here! Hold it right there!

54
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,451
Come here! Stop right there!

55
00:03:11,124 --> 00:03:12,693
When are the EXO guys coming?

56
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:13,794
Tell them to hurry!

57
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,863
How long do we have to wait?
What is this?

58
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,700
Why isn't it starting? What's going on?

59
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:24,271
Wait, did our boys get into
a car accident on the way here?

60
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:25,772
No way, that can't be!

61
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:27,441
-Let's pray!
-Right, pray!

62
00:04:19,126 --> 00:04:22,863
Let's go!

63
00:04:27,067 --> 00:04:30,570
Brush everything aside without fear

64
00:04:30,637 --> 00:04:33,273
Push forward boldly

65
00:04:34,307 --> 00:04:37,778
Negative words, faces, and lies

66
00:04:37,844 --> 00:04:41,114
Shout it out boldly

67
00:04:41,181 --> 00:04:44,651
Even if they call me a fool

68
00:04:44,718 --> 00:04:47,721
Even if they call me a psycho

69
00:04:47,788 --> 00:04:51,591
I'm better than you rich, smart phonies

70
00:04:51,658 --> 00:04:54,261
I'm a gutsy rock-and-roller

71
00:04:54,327 --> 00:04:58,832
I'll keep flooring it, so watch me

72
00:04:58,899 --> 00:05:01,334
Die! Die! Do or die!

73
00:05:01,401 --> 00:05:05,372
I'll do it my way, so watch me

74
00:05:05,438 --> 00:05:07,874
Die! Die! Do or die!

75
00:05:07,941 --> 00:05:11,878
Nobody can understand your life

76
00:05:11,945 --> 00:05:15,415
Live your life, be alive
Do it or die!

77
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:18,251
Ditch all the complicated stuff

78
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:22,823
I'll pull it all off, just watch me

79
00:05:41,308 --> 00:05:44,544
Back then, I was fearless.

80
00:05:45,712 --> 00:05:49,382
I thought I could achieve
anything I wanted.

81
00:05:51,785 --> 00:05:55,555
By my calculations,
even if I wasn't a superstar,

82
00:05:55,622 --> 00:05:58,491
I should've become
a pretty amazing adult.

83
00:06:05,265 --> 00:06:08,802
Nobody can understand your life

84
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:12,272
Live your life, be alive
Do it or die!

85
00:06:12,339 --> 00:06:15,275
Ditch all the complicated stuff

86
00:06:15,342 --> 00:06:19,880
I'll pull it all off, just watch me

87
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:24,618
EAT SOME CHILI & GREEN ONION PANCAKES!
CHILI FESTIVAL WOMEN'S CLUB

88
00:06:26,152 --> 00:06:28,288
But right now,

89
00:06:28,355 --> 00:06:32,025
I've become a pretty amazing loser.

90
00:06:32,092 --> 00:06:33,760
CHILI PEPPER FESTIVAL
GUEST EXO

91
00:06:36,596 --> 00:06:39,866
All right, that was our special guest,

92
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:41,902
the one-man rock band,

93
00:06:41,968 --> 00:06:44,304
EXO, with a fiery performance!

94
00:06:44,371 --> 00:06:46,339
Give it up for him!

95
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:48,208
Applause!

96
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,315
Good job.

97
00:07:01,788 --> 00:07:04,024
NATIONAL STARS
SPECIAL GUEST EXO

98
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:11,431
You said it was EXO! Is that thing EXO?

99
00:07:12,699 --> 00:07:14,801
Is that EXO, you little brat?

100
00:07:14,868 --> 00:07:18,104
Well, it was written on the banner…

101
00:07:18,171 --> 00:07:20,006
To look pretty for our boys,

102
00:07:20,073 --> 00:07:22,375
I curled my hair for two whole hours!

103
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:23,977
Wait, who even is that guy?

104
00:07:24,044 --> 00:07:27,881
How dare some nobody loser
impersonate our boys? Jeez!

105
00:07:27,948 --> 00:07:29,482
So annoying. Should I sue him?

106
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:32,352
Forget it, let it go.

107
00:07:32,419 --> 00:07:36,489
How broke must he be
to live like that at his age?

108
00:07:36,556 --> 00:07:39,259
Just leave the guy alone
to rot and croak.

109
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:43,730
Hey, let's go inhale some tteokbokki.

110
00:07:44,431 --> 00:07:47,467
Hey, School Uniform Killers 1, 2, and 3!

111
00:07:50,337 --> 00:07:51,838
What's he saying?

112
00:07:51,905 --> 00:07:54,474
Don't you feel sorry for your uniforms?

113
00:07:55,175 --> 00:07:57,777
Uniforms have feelings too, you brats!

114
00:07:59,579 --> 00:08:00,981
What's he talking about?

115
00:08:05,051 --> 00:08:07,120
Forget it, never mind.

116
00:08:07,187 --> 00:08:09,889
Why am I even talking to you?

117
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:16,229
Idol fangirls are truly
beyond help, I swear.

118
00:09:01,341 --> 00:09:02,575
Ow, it stings!

119
00:09:02,642 --> 00:09:05,145
Seriously, that stings!

120
00:09:07,113 --> 00:09:08,748
Those high school brats!

121
00:09:08,815 --> 00:09:10,683
I swear, I'm--

122
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:12,986
Argh!

123
00:09:25,265 --> 00:09:28,868
They paid me in chili peppers
instead of cash?

124
00:09:28,935 --> 00:09:32,739
You uncultured jerks have
zero respect for music!

125
00:09:33,773 --> 00:09:36,609
Seriously, what's wrong with this now?

126
00:10:08,875 --> 00:10:11,344
Why is my life like this?

127
00:10:22,188 --> 00:10:24,591
FOR YOUR APPROVAL

128
00:10:24,657 --> 00:10:26,059
Yes, Assistant Manager Kim.

129
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:29,129
I know how busy you are,
Assistant Manager Kim.

130
00:10:29,195 --> 00:10:30,864
But health checkups end this week,

131
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:34,334
so you really need to get yours
done by then. Yes.

132
00:10:35,001 --> 00:10:36,803
What? Really?

133
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:38,505
Thank you so much. Yes.

134
00:10:38,571 --> 00:10:40,673
Yes, thank you very much.

135
00:10:48,181 --> 00:10:49,482
HEALTH CHECKUP LIST

136
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:16,042
DAEJIN INDUSTRIAL
YOO HAN-CHEOL

137
00:11:30,023 --> 00:11:33,193
Hey, intern.
Why isn't my coffee here?

138
00:11:34,827 --> 00:11:37,197
I'm busy. Do I really have
to come get it myself?

139
00:11:47,974 --> 00:11:50,610
-Did the creamer clump?
-Yes, it clumped, sir.

140
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:54,747
Right, are the staff
health checkups all done?

141
00:11:54,814 --> 00:11:57,083
Yes, they're almost all done, sir.

142
00:11:57,150 --> 00:12:00,887
Whatever. Make sure every single
person gets it done this week.

143
00:12:02,088 --> 00:12:04,657
And I'm entertaining
clients tonight.

144
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:05,758
Help me out today.

145
00:12:05,825 --> 00:12:08,928
I'm not feeling well today, so I…

146
00:12:09,829 --> 00:12:11,331
Can't help it if you're sick.

147
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:14,133
But with a young guy
being so weak and sickly,

148
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:16,269
could you handle going full-time?

149
00:12:16,336 --> 00:12:19,539
Since you're unwell,
go home and get plenty of rest.

150
00:12:19,606 --> 00:12:21,741
Or you can rest forever.

151
00:12:21,808 --> 00:12:23,409
No, sir.

152
00:12:23,476 --> 00:12:26,012
I'll do it. Yes, I will.

153
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:30,617
Saying there's nothing more to give

154
00:12:30,683 --> 00:12:33,119
I lied to myself to come here

155
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:35,221
What is all this?

156
00:12:35,288 --> 00:12:37,357
Look at the state I'm in!

157
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:40,059
Where have the girls gone?

158
00:12:40,126 --> 00:12:41,995
JOB PREP CIVIL SERVICE ACADEMY

159
00:12:42,061 --> 00:12:43,997
Righteous armies led by the Northerners

160
00:12:44,063 --> 00:12:47,267
began springing up everywhere
to help Gwanghaegun.

161
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:49,969
A leading figure among them, now,

162
00:12:50,036 --> 00:12:52,238
also called the General in Red Robes,

163
00:12:52,305 --> 00:12:53,706
was Kwak Jae-u.

164
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:57,143
Next, Jo Sik's top disciple,

165
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:59,145
there was a guy named Jung In-hong.

166
00:12:59,212 --> 00:13:01,347
Kwak Jae-u and Jung In-hong.
Memorize these two.

167
00:13:01,414 --> 00:13:03,483
They were leading commanders
of the Northerners

168
00:13:03,549 --> 00:13:04,851
during the Imjin War.

169
00:13:04,917 --> 00:13:07,487
Now, Master Seosan Hyujeong,
active at Mount Myohyang,

170
00:13:07,553 --> 00:13:10,390
and Master Samyeong Yujeong,
at Mounts Taebaek and Geumgang.

171
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:12,925
With their help,
Gwanghaegun traveled around,

172
00:13:12,992 --> 00:13:16,896
winning back the public
and stabilizing society.

173
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:18,665
All right, that's all for today.

174
00:13:19,599 --> 00:13:20,466
Oh, right.

175
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:24,137
I almost forgot I have a gift
for you all today.

176
00:13:27,106 --> 00:13:29,409
The mock exam scores are out.

177
00:13:30,877 --> 00:13:32,578
All right, Jung Su-jin.

178
00:13:42,221 --> 00:13:44,223
TAKEOUT: 1 CHICKEN, 8,500 WON

179
00:13:50,930 --> 00:13:52,932
Stop it! Just stop, jeez!

180
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:55,134
You guys make me want to die too!

181
00:14:05,478 --> 00:14:08,081
If I fail this exam too, my dad says

182
00:14:09,048 --> 00:14:10,483
I have to work at his pig's feet shop.

183
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:12,685
It's driving me crazy, really.

184
00:14:14,654 --> 00:14:19,392
Be grateful you even have
a pig's feet shop to inherit, you punk.

185
00:14:25,498 --> 00:14:28,768
Hey, how long will you two
live like this?

186
00:14:28,835 --> 00:14:30,703
Isn't it time to wake up?

187
00:14:35,141 --> 00:14:39,379
Take the seaweed off your ear
before you lecture us, you bastard.

188
00:14:40,346 --> 00:14:42,348
You played backup
at a client party, huh?

189
00:14:42,415 --> 00:14:44,450
Entertaining clients is work, punk!

190
00:14:44,517 --> 00:14:48,388
Call it pro bono work
for the company, you punk.

191
00:14:48,454 --> 00:14:51,691
And you graciously did pro bono work
at a hostess bar, sir?

192
00:14:51,758 --> 00:14:54,394
Didn't you say you'd never
touch a guitar again?

193
00:14:55,128 --> 00:14:56,863
Do your pro bono work for me.

194
00:14:57,930 --> 00:14:58,831
That again?

195
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,900
Let's do the band one more time.

196
00:15:00,967 --> 00:15:03,136
Let's try just one last time.

197
00:15:03,202 --> 00:15:05,972
I already blasted our demo CD
to every agency.

198
00:15:06,038 --> 00:15:07,573
-So pretty soon…
-Hey.

199
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:09,909
We're 27 now. Twenty-seven!

200
00:15:09,976 --> 00:15:12,912
We're not 17 anymore,

201
00:15:12,979 --> 00:15:14,781
when the whole sky looked blue!

202
00:15:14,847 --> 00:15:17,083
We're not, we're not, we're not!

203
00:15:17,150 --> 00:15:20,553
Besides, what agency
would put out our album?

204
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:23,055
They'd rather make
another handsome idol with that money.

205
00:15:23,122 --> 00:15:27,026
Hey! If they won't,
we'll make it ourselves, punk!

206
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:29,662
How much does it cost
to produce and promote it?

207
00:15:29,729 --> 00:15:32,698
Right, 100 million! That's all it takes.

208
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:33,800
A hundred million?

209
00:15:33,866 --> 00:15:36,903
Think 100 million is game money
from typing "show me the money"?

210
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:42,875
Whether you learn a trade
or get a job,

211
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,377
figure out how to survive.

212
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:46,879
And quit music.

213
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:49,348
"Quit" is only for counting
heads of cabbage!

214
00:15:49,415 --> 00:15:53,186
I've put in way too much
to ever quit now!

215
00:15:53,252 --> 00:15:55,254
You just wait and see.

216
00:15:55,321 --> 00:15:57,223
I'll make it big for sure

217
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:59,959
and play Carnegie Hall in New York!

218
00:16:05,665 --> 00:16:06,899
Carnegie Hall?

219
00:16:07,934 --> 00:16:10,470
Just stuff your face with puffed corn!

220
00:16:10,536 --> 00:16:12,605
When will you grow up? Oh, my…

221
00:16:16,742 --> 00:16:17,877
Ow, my stomach.

222
00:16:17,944 --> 00:16:19,278
Why does it hurt so much?

223
00:16:19,345 --> 00:16:21,881
Again? Just go see a doctor.

224
00:16:21,948 --> 00:16:23,282
Don't tough it out to save a few bucks.

225
00:16:23,349 --> 00:16:25,384
Actually, I got tested a few days ago.

226
00:16:25,451 --> 00:16:28,688
Oh, I saw Hyeok at the hospital. Hyeok.

227
00:16:28,754 --> 00:16:31,858
In a white coat, an intern
or whatever…

228
00:16:31,924 --> 00:16:33,993
Damn it! Seriously!

229
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,895
-You scared me!
-Come on!

230
00:16:35,962 --> 00:16:38,064
Why bring up that bastard
and ruin my drink?

231
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:40,800
Don't you know who put us
in this pathetic mess?

232
00:16:40,867 --> 00:16:42,568
Unbelievable.

233
00:16:42,635 --> 00:16:44,604
This world is so screwed up. Damn.

234
00:16:46,239 --> 00:16:47,607
Huh?

235
00:16:52,078 --> 00:16:56,082
Yu-na's still so pretty,
and still doing great.

236
00:16:56,148 --> 00:16:57,783
Tell me about it.

237
00:16:57,850 --> 00:16:59,886
Does she eat preservatives
for three meals a day?

238
00:16:59,952 --> 00:17:01,621
She never ages, right?

239
00:17:03,723 --> 00:17:08,261
Hey, why are you suddenly
cosplaying a tragic hero?

240
00:17:08,327 --> 00:17:11,197
Hey, are you still not over her?

241
00:17:12,798 --> 00:17:14,200
Wake up, punk.

242
00:17:14,267 --> 00:17:17,770
For guys like us,
Yu-na's been way out of reach

243
00:17:17,837 --> 00:17:19,772
for a long time now, punk.

244
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:21,941
Hey, what's wrong? Where are you going?

245
00:17:22,008 --> 00:17:23,276
Punk!

246
00:17:26,579 --> 00:17:28,014
You went too far.

247
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:29,615
Why provoke Min-gi like that?

248
00:17:29,682 --> 00:17:31,884
So he'd know his place. What?

249
00:17:31,951 --> 00:17:33,953
And when did I ever provoke him?

250
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:36,389
Throwing a fit and overreacting
like this…

251
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:38,457
Wait a second.

252
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:47,633
Hey! Pay for your drinks first,
you jerk!

253
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:49,602
Oh, you really!

254
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,475
We said we'd split it, you bastard!

255
00:17:56,542 --> 00:17:57,910
You cheap jerk!

256
00:17:57,977 --> 00:18:00,780
What's wrong with that guy, seriously?

257
00:18:00,846 --> 00:18:02,481
Right, Ki-jun…

258
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,697
Hey!

259
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:20,066
I really hate you guys!

260
00:18:20,132 --> 00:18:22,101
More than my bank balance!

261
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:55,368
DEWY MOISTURIZING EFFECT
YUJIN

262
00:19:26,032 --> 00:19:27,066
HANYOUNG BANK
URGENT NOTICE

263
00:20:10,009 --> 00:20:13,012
It's fine. I didn't put ice in it.

264
00:20:13,079 --> 00:20:15,181
Just so you know,

265
00:20:15,247 --> 00:20:17,650
I really hate it when people drag on.

266
00:20:17,717 --> 00:20:20,252
From now on, keep every answer

267
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:22,655
to five syllables or less, okay?

268
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:27,526
The way I see it,
you're either a genius or an idiot.

269
00:20:27,593 --> 00:20:29,895
Of all the guys who took my money,

270
00:20:29,962 --> 00:20:31,464
some fled to a remote island,

271
00:20:31,530 --> 00:20:33,799
and some fled overseas,

272
00:20:33,866 --> 00:20:37,403
but you're the first to flee
right next door to your old place.

273
00:20:38,270 --> 00:20:41,140
Man, thanks to you,
I looked in all the wrong places

274
00:20:41,207 --> 00:20:42,742
and spent a ton on gas.

275
00:20:42,808 --> 00:20:44,677
No, I didn't do it on purpose.

276
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:48,214
I was behind on rent,
so I had no choice but to move next door.

277
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:50,015
So I had no choice--

278
00:20:58,357 --> 00:20:59,725
I said keep it short.

279
00:21:00,693 --> 00:21:01,894
Did you forget already?

280
00:21:01,961 --> 00:21:03,629
How many syllables max?

281
00:21:03,696 --> 00:21:05,264
Five syllables.

282
00:21:05,331 --> 00:21:06,799
That's right.

283
00:21:06,866 --> 00:21:10,302
When your head is dumb,
your body pays the price.

284
00:21:10,369 --> 00:21:12,571
Use your fingers. Your fingers.

285
00:21:12,638 --> 00:21:14,006
That's it.

286
00:21:15,241 --> 00:21:19,311
Cut the crap. My 70 million won.

287
00:21:19,378 --> 00:21:22,915
Oh, wait, no.
It's 100 million now. A hundred million.

288
00:21:22,982 --> 00:21:24,683
When will you pay it back?

289
00:21:25,484 --> 00:21:26,752
This is crazy.

290
00:21:28,788 --> 00:21:30,222
Catch the

291
00:21:33,392 --> 00:21:35,060
con man.

292
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:37,730
The con man?

293
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:40,032
Oh, the guy who took your money and ran,

294
00:21:40,099 --> 00:21:42,735
that agency boss? You'll pay
when you catch him?

295
00:21:42,802 --> 00:21:46,539
Man, this bastard is something else
when it comes to creativity.

296
00:21:47,339 --> 00:21:48,574
That agency boss

297
00:21:48,641 --> 00:21:51,377
wouldn't still have your money now,

298
00:21:51,443 --> 00:21:54,747
and why the hell should I
wait around for that?

299
00:21:56,448 --> 00:21:58,317
Cut me some

300
00:22:06,959 --> 00:22:08,360
Cut me a break.

301
00:22:18,871 --> 00:22:21,841
Did this punk just talk down to me?

302
00:22:22,608 --> 00:22:26,445
I'll ask one last time.
When will you pay back my money?

303
00:22:28,547 --> 00:22:30,516
Within a year, sir.

304
00:22:30,583 --> 00:22:32,218
Still hasn't come to his senses.

305
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:34,286
No good, boys.

306
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:36,121
-Yes, sir.
-Give the punk surgery.

307
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,556
-Yes, sir.
-Surgery?

308
00:22:37,623 --> 00:22:40,492
Don't worry. We don't need
a guardian's consent.

309
00:22:40,559 --> 00:22:41,961
-Pull!
-Yes, sir.

310
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:44,163
Boss, boss! Give me a little time!

311
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:46,332
Hey! Let go!

312
00:22:46,398 --> 00:22:48,767
I'm signing with an agency
and dropping an album,

313
00:22:48,834 --> 00:22:50,269
so 100 million is noth--

314
00:22:52,605 --> 00:22:54,974
Please let me off once!
Just once, boss!

315
00:23:00,613 --> 00:23:03,582
Spare me, spare me!
I'll pay you back! Wait, wait!

316
00:23:10,856 --> 00:23:13,225
Boss, I really can pay you back!

317
00:23:13,292 --> 00:23:14,493
-I'll pay--
-Hey, stop.

318
00:23:15,761 --> 00:23:17,863
-I can't breathe.
-Stop.

319
00:23:17,930 --> 00:23:19,665
I really can't breathe.

320
00:23:19,732 --> 00:23:21,333
Stop!

321
00:23:24,303 --> 00:23:26,672
Hey, where did you get THIS?

322
00:23:28,374 --> 00:23:29,308
Well?

323
00:23:30,709 --> 00:23:32,945
Not stolen.

324
00:23:33,712 --> 00:23:36,515
I didn't say you stole it!
Where did you get it?

325
00:23:38,884 --> 00:23:40,953
As a kid…

326
00:23:42,788 --> 00:23:44,123
found it.

327
00:23:44,189 --> 00:23:45,824
You're driving me nuts!

328
00:23:45,891 --> 00:23:48,560
Talk as long as you want!
Give me the details, punk!

329
00:23:48,627 --> 00:23:50,029
Yes, okay.

330
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,931
I found it on a mountain
as a kid.

331
00:23:51,997 --> 00:23:53,232
Some guy left it behind.

332
00:23:53,299 --> 00:23:55,134
A guy? What guy?

333
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,835
I don't really know.

334
00:23:58,304 --> 00:24:01,273
Boss, just give me a year,
no, six months.

335
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:04,643
I swear on my life
I will definitely pay you back, boss.

336
00:24:04,710 --> 00:24:07,079
Boss, out of the goodness
of your big heart,

337
00:24:07,146 --> 00:24:08,013
-boss--
-Quiet.

338
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:08,948
Yes, sir.

339
00:24:09,014 --> 00:24:10,249
-Three months.
-What?

340
00:24:10,316 --> 00:24:11,550
Pay up by then, hear?

341
00:24:16,755 --> 00:24:19,024
Thank you, thank you!

342
00:24:23,262 --> 00:24:25,831
Boss, what came over you all of a sudden?

343
00:24:25,898 --> 00:24:27,132
How can you trust him?

344
00:24:32,438 --> 00:24:33,472
Nothing.

345
00:24:35,074 --> 00:24:37,509
It just brought back old memories.

346
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:42,014
Let's go.

347
00:25:22,054 --> 00:25:23,489
Hello?

348
00:25:24,256 --> 00:25:25,591
Who is this?

349
00:25:29,762 --> 00:25:30,629
What?

350
00:25:30,696 --> 00:25:32,831
FUNERAL HOME

351
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:37,002
-Thanks for your hard work.
-Eat up.

352
00:25:40,239 --> 00:25:42,641
Why did nobody show up?

353
00:25:43,442 --> 00:25:45,210
This is everyone.

354
00:25:45,277 --> 00:25:46,979
Everyone? What do you mean?

355
00:25:47,046 --> 00:25:49,348
The old lady had one nasty temper.

356
00:25:49,415 --> 00:25:51,950
Folks shook their heads
just passing her in town,

357
00:25:52,017 --> 00:25:53,052
so why come here?

358
00:25:53,118 --> 00:25:55,087
Still, people should come for a funeral.

359
00:25:55,154 --> 00:25:57,156
That's not right.

360
00:25:57,222 --> 00:25:59,892
What do we do without a chief mourner?

361
00:25:59,958 --> 00:26:01,693
Park Sang-deuk called, so he'll come.

362
00:26:03,362 --> 00:26:04,263
Fat chance.

363
00:26:04,329 --> 00:26:06,465
If they were the type to come here,

364
00:26:06,532 --> 00:26:09,601
they wouldn't have fled in the night
and left the old lady behind.

365
00:26:10,369 --> 00:26:13,505
Then again, I wouldn't come either.

366
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:15,074
After her son died in the typhoon,

367
00:26:15,140 --> 00:26:17,209
Granny Kim gave her daughter-in-law
such a hard time,

368
00:26:17,276 --> 00:26:19,445
calling her a bitch who killed her son.

369
00:26:19,511 --> 00:26:21,513
She brought it on herself.

370
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:24,583
She's passed away now.
How can you keep talking like--

371
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:26,618
Am I wrong?

372
00:26:26,685 --> 00:26:28,687
You always snap at me.

373
00:26:29,988 --> 00:26:31,690
Bring me a pint of draft.

374
00:26:32,991 --> 00:26:34,393
Cheers!

375
00:26:37,229 --> 00:26:40,165
That guy is guzzling booze
even in his dreams.

376
00:26:40,232 --> 00:26:41,533
Drink up.

377
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,902
GRANDPA MUSCLE

378
00:26:43,969 --> 00:26:47,239
He cared so much about his health.
How could he…

379
00:26:47,739 --> 00:26:50,142
Tell me about it.
He worked out so much.

380
00:26:50,209 --> 00:26:52,377
Swimming, hiking, ping-pong, baseball…

381
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:54,713
What else? Right, boxing.

382
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:57,516
STREET FIGHTER MMA…

383
00:26:58,383 --> 00:26:59,251
Hey.

384
00:26:59,318 --> 00:27:00,185
MMA CLUB

385
00:27:00,252 --> 00:27:01,487
Hey, hold on.

386
00:27:01,553 --> 00:27:02,921
What are you doing? Come out.

387
00:27:02,988 --> 00:27:05,691
Gosh, let go of me.

388
00:27:05,757 --> 00:27:07,326
Hands off a lady!

389
00:27:07,392 --> 00:27:08,861
A lady?

390
00:27:08,927 --> 00:27:10,762
Why's a lady stealing a wreath?

391
00:27:10,829 --> 00:27:12,664
Stealing it?

392
00:27:12,731 --> 00:27:14,967
I was just going to borrow it
for a bit.

393
00:27:15,033 --> 00:27:17,035
Who do you take me for?

394
00:27:17,102 --> 00:27:21,006
Why are you borrowing a wreath
from someone else's funeral?

395
00:27:22,074 --> 00:27:23,342
Mister.

396
00:27:25,043 --> 00:27:26,345
Look over there.

397
00:27:26,411 --> 00:27:29,081
Don't you feel a pang in your heart?

398
00:27:29,148 --> 00:27:30,249
I don't feel a thing.

399
00:27:30,315 --> 00:27:32,251
The rich get richer, the poor poorer!

400
00:27:32,317 --> 00:27:34,086
Don't you feel that?

401
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:36,555
They've got a whole flower expo
going on over here,

402
00:27:36,622 --> 00:27:39,424
while our place looks like a wasteland.

403
00:27:39,925 --> 00:27:43,262
Our poor Granny Kim
had such a hard life before she died.

404
00:27:43,328 --> 00:27:45,631
With just one wreath out front,

405
00:27:45,697 --> 00:27:48,033
guests would feel good
and Granny would save face.

406
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:49,034
Everyone wins!

407
00:27:49,101 --> 00:27:50,969
Then go buy one yourself, miss.

408
00:27:51,036 --> 00:27:51,904
Gosh, mister.

409
00:27:51,970 --> 00:27:54,039
Flowers are overflowing everywhere here,

410
00:27:54,106 --> 00:27:55,641
so why waste money?

411
00:27:55,707 --> 00:27:57,109
Frankly, the deceased

412
00:27:57,176 --> 00:27:59,011
isn't going to smell them
on the way out,

413
00:27:59,077 --> 00:28:02,414
so think of it as doing
a good deed today

414
00:28:02,481 --> 00:28:05,317
and lend me just one wreath.

415
00:28:07,419 --> 00:28:09,821
Come on, if you really hate the idea…

416
00:28:10,589 --> 00:28:14,092
Still, lend me just one, please?

417
00:28:14,159 --> 00:28:16,662
STREET…

418
00:28:16,728 --> 00:28:20,532
REST IN PEACE

419
00:28:24,770 --> 00:28:26,705
Hello?

420
00:28:27,539 --> 00:28:30,108
Me? I'm at the funeral home.

421
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:32,377
What? Hye-gyo and Tae-hui?

422
00:28:32,444 --> 00:28:34,012
Ma'am, ma'am!

423
00:28:34,980 --> 00:28:36,248
What's all the fuss?

424
00:28:36,315 --> 00:28:38,717
Hye-gyo and Tae-hui are having babies!

425
00:28:38,784 --> 00:28:40,085
Babies?

426
00:28:40,152 --> 00:28:43,088
Gosh, our cows, our cows!
They're calving!

427
00:28:43,155 --> 00:28:46,024
Once I go back,
I might not make it back here,

428
00:28:46,091 --> 00:28:49,127
so tell Sang-deok to wrap up
the funeral nicely.

429
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:50,729
-Got it.
-I'm off.

430
00:28:50,796 --> 00:28:52,664
-Go on.
-Hey, be careful!

431
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:55,133
Hye-gyo, Tae-hui, hang on!
Mommy's coming!

432
00:28:58,537 --> 00:28:59,805
Gosh, I'm so sorry.

433
00:28:59,871 --> 00:29:02,341
I'm in a huge rush.
Oh, no, what do I do!

434
00:29:07,379 --> 00:29:10,349
My sunglasses, my sunglasses!

435
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:15,854
What are you going to do about this?

436
00:29:15,921 --> 00:29:18,790
I worked part-time
for a whole year

437
00:29:18,857 --> 00:29:21,426
just to buy these sunglasses!
What'll you do!

438
00:29:22,794 --> 00:29:24,563
You clearly look younger than me,

439
00:29:24,630 --> 00:29:26,932
so watch your mouth, huh?

440
00:29:26,999 --> 00:29:29,801
I'll pay for them, okay?
How much are they?

441
00:29:30,535 --> 00:29:32,871
Gosh, 20,000 won? Come on.

442
00:29:32,938 --> 00:29:35,507
I'll pay you back.
20,000 won is no big deal.

443
00:29:35,574 --> 00:29:36,441
Two million.

444
00:29:40,679 --> 00:29:42,981
Two million?

445
00:29:43,048 --> 00:29:45,284
What, two million won?

446
00:29:46,084 --> 00:29:49,354
What kind of sunglasses
cost two million won?

447
00:29:53,392 --> 00:29:55,894
-Your 100-meter time?
-What?

448
00:29:55,961 --> 00:29:58,063
How fast do you run 100 meters?

449
00:29:58,997 --> 00:30:00,299
14 seconds?

450
00:30:01,500 --> 00:30:03,769
-Why do you ask?
-I run it in 12 seconds.

451
00:30:08,874 --> 00:30:12,277
Hey! Come here! Come back here!

452
00:30:12,344 --> 00:30:13,512
Hey, get back here!

453
00:30:13,578 --> 00:30:15,013
Stop! Stop!

454
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:16,281
Hey! Hey!

455
00:30:19,518 --> 00:30:20,686
What is that?

456
00:30:21,453 --> 00:30:22,721
Sorry!

457
00:30:25,924 --> 00:30:28,960
Hey! Stop right there!
Don't go! Don't go!

458
00:30:30,962 --> 00:30:33,265
Hey! 4885!

459
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:36,301
It's so lonely in here.

460
00:30:36,368 --> 00:30:37,969
I told you that was all of them.

461
00:30:51,950 --> 00:30:53,051
This is my grandmother.

462
00:30:53,118 --> 00:30:54,152
THE LATE KIM BOK-SUN

463
00:30:54,219 --> 00:30:56,254
With the sweetest face in the world,

464
00:30:56,321 --> 00:30:58,824
she boasted a tongue
as savage as Kim Gu-ra's.

465
00:30:58,890 --> 00:31:00,025
My grandmother.

466
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:04,029
Guess I won't get chewed out anymore.

467
00:31:06,765 --> 00:31:09,101
Still, she could've lived
a little longer.

468
00:31:34,059 --> 00:31:36,528
-Are you Min-gi?
-Good grief!

469
00:31:36,595 --> 00:31:38,363
Look how big this kid got.

470
00:31:38,430 --> 00:31:43,435
Seems like just yesterday you were
running around with a runny nose.

471
00:31:43,502 --> 00:31:45,170
-Who are you?
-You punk.

472
00:31:45,237 --> 00:31:47,205
It's me, Sang-deuk, you punk!

473
00:31:47,873 --> 00:31:51,143
I lived in the big tile-roofed house
by the well. Don't you remember?

474
00:31:51,209 --> 00:31:54,679
When you fell out of that tree,
I rubbed soybean paste on you, kid.

475
00:31:54,746 --> 00:31:55,814
And I caught earwigs for you, punk.

476
00:31:55,881 --> 00:31:58,984
-So what do you want?
-Right.

477
00:32:00,519 --> 00:32:02,788
I had something to tell you.
What was it?

478
00:32:04,156 --> 00:32:06,458
I swear, I need to quit
this damn booze.

479
00:32:07,325 --> 00:32:09,461
Let's talk when you're sober.

480
00:32:13,298 --> 00:32:14,900
The inheritance!

481
00:32:14,966 --> 00:32:16,568
Your grandma's inheritance.

482
00:32:18,570 --> 00:32:22,174
Your grandma left you
an inheritance.

483
00:32:24,609 --> 00:32:25,777
Oh, Sang-deuk!

484
00:32:25,844 --> 00:32:28,146
Goodness, Sang-deuk!
My dear brother Sang-deuk!

485
00:32:28,213 --> 00:32:29,281
What took you so long?

486
00:32:29,347 --> 00:32:31,550
You didn't rub soybean paste
on me back then.

487
00:32:32,551 --> 00:32:34,753
Wait, so my grandma…

488
00:32:34,820 --> 00:32:37,556
Did she leave her estate
with a realtor or something?

489
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:38,657
Or collect art?

490
00:32:38,723 --> 00:32:42,661
It's nothing much.
Just a tiny little patch of field.

491
00:32:42,727 --> 00:32:45,263
About 10,000 pyeong, maybe?

492
00:32:48,900 --> 00:32:50,936
10,000 pyeong!

493
00:32:52,170 --> 00:32:56,775
Wait, not 100 pyeong,
not 1,000, but 10,000 pyeong?

494
00:32:56,842 --> 00:32:58,143
Wait, what's that mean?

495
00:32:58,210 --> 00:33:01,847
Even at 10,000 won per pyeong,
10,000 pyeong is 100 million won!

496
00:33:01,913 --> 00:33:03,548
At 100,000 won…

497
00:33:04,049 --> 00:33:06,051
One billion won!

498
00:33:06,885 --> 00:33:11,323
Gosh, after stressing me out
for so long,

499
00:33:11,389 --> 00:33:14,259
you hit me with the jackpot
all at once!

500
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:17,596
Thank you, Lord!
No, thank you, Grandma!

501
00:33:17,662 --> 00:33:19,164
Thank you so much!

502
00:33:21,032 --> 00:33:22,234
THE LATE KIM BOK-SUN

503
00:33:24,803 --> 00:33:26,271
Grandma!

504
00:33:29,207 --> 00:33:31,009
Grandma!

505
00:33:35,614 --> 00:33:38,183
Her grandson must've cared
for her deeply.

506
00:33:38,250 --> 00:33:40,018
Grandma…

507
00:33:40,085 --> 00:33:42,487
He's bawling his eyes out.

508
00:33:42,554 --> 00:33:44,556
Grandma…

509
00:34:03,909 --> 00:34:06,278
You said we were there.
How much farther up is it?

510
00:34:10,515 --> 00:34:12,017
Right here.

511
00:34:12,083 --> 00:34:13,885
How is it?

512
00:34:26,965 --> 00:34:29,334
It's huge. So huge.

513
00:34:29,401 --> 00:34:31,836
No, it's vast.

514
00:34:32,571 --> 00:34:36,207
10,000 pyeong really is massive.

515
00:34:36,274 --> 00:34:40,645
The soil here is so rich,
cabbages grow like crazy.

516
00:34:40,712 --> 00:34:45,550
Come fall, when this whole field
is packed tight with cabbages,

517
00:34:45,617 --> 00:34:47,385
the view is just killer.

518
00:34:48,587 --> 00:34:50,522
Fresh cabbage kimchi with makgeolli…

519
00:34:50,589 --> 00:34:53,425
Down a bowl of makgeolli right here,
and man…

520
00:34:54,292 --> 00:34:55,760
Mister.

521
00:34:55,827 --> 00:34:58,163
Do you know a realtor around here?

522
00:35:01,766 --> 00:35:04,402
-Don't tell me you're selling it?
-Yes.

523
00:35:04,469 --> 00:35:07,105
Your grandma farmed this land
her whole life.

524
00:35:07,739 --> 00:35:08,840
Must you sell it?

525
00:35:09,608 --> 00:35:11,743
If I don't sell it,
I'm dead, mister.

526
00:35:13,144 --> 00:35:15,614
If I just leave it like this…

527
00:35:17,482 --> 00:35:19,784
it'll remind me of Grandma
too much.

528
00:35:21,219 --> 00:35:23,221
I want Grandma to stop worrying
about the field

529
00:35:23,288 --> 00:35:25,457
and rest in peace now.

530
00:35:29,861 --> 00:35:32,897
By the way, how much does
this land go for…

531
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:34,699
Let's see…

532
00:35:34,766 --> 00:35:37,702
About 200 these days?

533
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:42,173
Two million won?

534
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:43,908
No, 200 won.

535
00:35:46,611 --> 00:35:47,812
No way.

536
00:35:47,879 --> 00:35:51,182
So even if I sell all 10,000 pyeong,
it's only two million won?

537
00:35:53,051 --> 00:35:54,819
Come on, you're joking, right?

538
00:35:54,886 --> 00:35:56,421
I'm not joking.

539
00:35:56,488 --> 00:35:58,790
At its peak, it went up to 300 won.

540
00:35:58,857 --> 00:35:59,891
Plus,

541
00:35:59,958 --> 00:36:03,094
this is the most remote spot
in the whole village.

542
00:36:03,161 --> 00:36:04,696
So it's really 200 won?

543
00:36:04,763 --> 00:36:08,700
I'm telling you, it is.
All the land around here costs that.

544
00:36:08,767 --> 00:36:11,269
Selling it won't get you
any real money.

545
00:36:18,410 --> 00:36:20,478
Min-gi, what's wrong with you?

546
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:27,352
Are you crying?

547
00:36:28,653 --> 00:36:30,088
Wait, why?

548
00:36:32,223 --> 00:36:34,592
It's time to let your grandma go.

549
00:36:36,061 --> 00:36:38,163
You're gonna make me cry too.

550
00:36:41,633 --> 00:36:42,901
Get up.

551
00:36:44,803 --> 00:36:46,504
100 WON

552
00:36:50,542 --> 00:36:52,077
OX BONE SOUP, BEEF BRISKET SOUP

553
00:37:22,974 --> 00:37:24,075
Lower your eyes.

554
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:27,345
Before you get fired.

555
00:37:29,614 --> 00:37:32,951
I told you to do the dishes first.
Why are you still slacking off?

556
00:37:35,420 --> 00:37:38,490
Do the dishes later
and trim the cabbages first.

557
00:37:38,556 --> 00:37:39,791
Fine!

558
00:37:41,760 --> 00:37:43,428
Just go away!

559
00:37:59,677 --> 00:38:01,479
What now? Why?

560
00:38:01,546 --> 00:38:04,315
One head of this costs 3,000 won!
3,000 won!

561
00:38:04,382 --> 00:38:06,451
If you rip all the leaves off,
what'll we make kimchi with?

562
00:38:07,418 --> 00:38:08,586
Go do your own work.

563
00:38:13,091 --> 00:38:15,293
I'm so sick of rising prices.

564
00:38:16,261 --> 00:38:20,198
How crazy will kimchi cabbage prices
get this fall?

565
00:38:21,199 --> 00:38:24,702
It's not cabbage anymore.
It's pure gold. Green gold.

566
00:38:25,570 --> 00:38:27,705
Wait, cabbage?

567
00:38:27,772 --> 00:38:29,841
Cabbage is green gold?

568
00:38:29,908 --> 00:38:33,778
The soil here is so rich,
cabbages grow like crazy.

569
00:38:33,845 --> 00:38:35,547
Come fall,

570
00:38:35,613 --> 00:38:39,284
when this whole field
is packed tight with cabbages,

571
00:38:39,350 --> 00:38:41,820
the view is just killer.

572
00:38:52,697 --> 00:38:53,932
CABBAGE FARMING

573
00:39:05,109 --> 00:39:06,211
CABBAGE PRICES

574
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:12,784
HISTORY OF CABBAGE FARMING

575
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:16,554
FALL CABBAGE UP 20%, CRASH FEARED

576
00:39:16,621 --> 00:39:20,825
"Cabbage prices repeat a cycle
of surging and crashing every two years,

577
00:39:20,892 --> 00:39:22,227
the two-year cycle…"

578
00:39:23,962 --> 00:39:26,397
Two-year cycle? What's that?

579
00:39:32,670 --> 00:39:35,206
2010, cabbage prices surge.

580
00:39:35,273 --> 00:39:37,942
What? 15,000 won a head?

581
00:39:38,009 --> 00:39:40,979
2011, cabbage prices crash.

582
00:39:41,045 --> 00:39:43,982
2012, cabbage prices surge.

583
00:39:44,048 --> 00:39:46,351
2013, cabbage prices crash.

584
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:50,555
What is this?

585
00:39:50,622 --> 00:39:52,190
Every two years, prices really

586
00:39:52,257 --> 00:39:54,592
keep surging and crashing!

587
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:59,597
Say a head goes for about 10,000 won
during a surge,

588
00:39:59,664 --> 00:40:02,300
and I plant one head per pyeong.

589
00:40:02,367 --> 00:40:05,703
It's 10,000 pyeong,
so 10,000 heads…

590
00:40:05,770 --> 00:40:08,273
10,000 heads times 10,000 won is…

591
00:40:09,607 --> 00:40:11,509
100 million won! Wait, wait.

592
00:40:11,576 --> 00:40:16,014
I can plant at least ten heads
per pyeong, right?

593
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:18,850
100,000 heads times 10,000 won is…

594
00:40:23,154 --> 00:40:24,489
One billion won!

595
00:40:39,837 --> 00:40:42,807
At last, the light of dawn
shines upon my life!

596
00:40:46,744 --> 00:40:48,613
Hold on.

597
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:50,682
How do I plant 100,000 cabbages alone?

598
00:40:50,748 --> 00:40:53,418
Where can I find guys
with nothing to do, gullible,

599
00:40:53,484 --> 00:40:56,187
and strong, useless slackers?

600
00:40:59,924 --> 00:41:01,592
Wait, I know some.

601
00:41:01,659 --> 00:41:02,694
I definitely do.

602
00:41:09,968 --> 00:41:12,103
I have to stop by the hospital too.

603
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:15,039
Come on, seriously.

604
00:41:16,140 --> 00:41:18,042
No one even woke me up.

605
00:41:20,545 --> 00:41:23,348
Darn it, I'm in such a rush.

606
00:41:36,627 --> 00:41:38,997
Come eat, you little brats!

607
00:41:39,063 --> 00:41:41,032
Yes, coming!

608
00:42:09,494 --> 00:42:10,528
So spicy.

609
00:42:12,230 --> 00:42:15,666
Starting today, we eat only peppers.

610
00:42:16,768 --> 00:42:18,803
Still, this is a bit much…

611
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:22,540
Who told you to bring home
a whole sack of peppers?

612
00:42:22,607 --> 00:42:24,509
Look at that.

613
00:42:24,575 --> 00:42:26,611
Min-gi told me to bring them to you.

614
00:42:26,677 --> 00:42:27,845
Min-gi?

615
00:42:28,780 --> 00:42:32,483
That good-for-nothing punk
who ruined your life?

616
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:35,520
Are you still hanging out
with that jerk?

617
00:42:35,586 --> 00:42:37,288
No, I just bumped into him.

618
00:42:37,355 --> 00:42:39,424
He was just carrying peppers
on the street.

619
00:42:39,490 --> 00:42:42,660
Why isn't this freeloader
out of his room yet?

620
00:42:43,461 --> 00:42:47,799
Yoo Han-gi! Didn't you hear me
call you for breakfast?

621
00:42:49,967 --> 00:42:52,270
Didn't I tell you not to even
touch a guitar?

622
00:42:52,336 --> 00:42:54,238
-Didn't I?
-I didn't do anything!

623
00:42:54,305 --> 00:42:58,209
Do you want to end up
like that piece of trash too?

624
00:42:58,276 --> 00:42:59,844
Come on, stop it, Mom!

625
00:42:59,911 --> 00:43:03,114
Does strumming a guitar
put food on the table?

626
00:43:03,181 --> 00:43:04,382
Or pay the bills?

627
00:43:04,449 --> 00:43:05,550
HANKOOK HOSPITAL

628
00:43:06,517 --> 00:43:08,286
W-w-what's wrong with these guys?

629
00:43:08,352 --> 00:43:10,121
They shouldn't be like this.

630
00:43:17,195 --> 00:43:19,030
Um, I… Is it bad?

631
00:43:19,097 --> 00:43:21,432
SPECIALIST SEOK JIK-GU

632
00:43:21,499 --> 00:43:24,268
Should I beat around the bush
and keep it vague?

633
00:43:24,335 --> 00:43:27,839
Or would you rather I give it to you
straight and honest?

634
00:43:27,905 --> 00:43:31,642
Um, if you could just give it to me
straight and honest…

635
00:43:31,709 --> 00:43:34,045
It's cancer. Liver cancer.
Stage four.

636
00:43:34,112 --> 00:43:35,913
Too late for surgery.

637
00:43:35,980 --> 00:43:37,949
If I wanted money, I'd say operate.

638
00:43:38,015 --> 00:43:40,284
We'd just cut you open
and sew you right back up.

639
00:43:44,689 --> 00:43:46,090
Um, right now, I--

640
00:43:47,125 --> 00:43:49,594
-Me?
-Optimistically, one year.

641
00:43:49,660 --> 00:43:50,828
Six months on average.

642
00:43:50,895 --> 00:43:51,996
Unlucky, three months.

643
00:43:52,063 --> 00:43:54,031
Even unluckier, could be tomorrow.

644
00:43:54,098 --> 00:43:56,567
U-um, I, so you mean I'm…

645
00:43:57,969 --> 00:44:00,138
Are you saying I'm terminally ill?

646
00:44:00,905 --> 00:44:03,274
In other words,
your days are numbered.

647
00:44:03,341 --> 00:44:05,676
Though that sounds a bit cruel.

648
00:44:06,544 --> 00:44:09,981
I really hate beating around the bush.

649
00:44:10,047 --> 00:44:11,949
If you'd just gotten regular checkups,

650
00:44:12,016 --> 00:44:14,585
it wouldn't have gotten this bad.

651
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:18,189
Look at these guys. Gosh,
this is bad, huh?

652
00:44:19,290 --> 00:44:22,493
Why on earth didn't you get
a health checkup?

653
00:44:23,961 --> 00:44:25,429
Well…

654
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:30,334
I'm a contract worker.

655
00:44:30,401 --> 00:44:33,437
A contract-- Gosh.

656
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:35,072
Are these guys temp workers too?

657
00:44:35,139 --> 00:44:36,941
Usually… Oh, dear.

658
00:44:37,008 --> 00:44:38,476
These guys are so weird.

659
00:45:41,172 --> 00:45:43,374
I'M TAEBAEK GEUMSEONG!
BIG TROUBLE! PANT, PANT

660
00:45:43,441 --> 00:45:44,642
WHY DID HE SHRINK?

661
00:46:04,028 --> 00:46:06,230
Hey, intern! What time is it?

662
00:46:06,297 --> 00:46:09,567
You said you had a quick errand.
What time is it now?

663
00:46:10,768 --> 00:46:12,436
-I'm sorry.
-Forget it.

664
00:46:12,503 --> 00:46:15,139
You know staff health checkups
are due tomorrow, right?

665
00:46:15,206 --> 00:46:18,643
If even one person misses it,
we're both dead meat, got it?

666
00:46:33,724 --> 00:46:35,660
HEALTH CHECKUP LIST

667
00:46:48,039 --> 00:46:49,707
Hello, Assistant Manager Kim.

668
00:46:51,108 --> 00:46:52,910
Did you get your checkup?

669
00:46:54,445 --> 00:46:56,747
I know you're very busy,

670
00:46:57,448 --> 00:47:00,117
but the checkup deadline is tomorrow,

671
00:47:00,184 --> 00:47:02,653
so you really need to get it by…

672
00:47:09,760 --> 00:47:11,395
Why on earth!

673
00:47:11,462 --> 00:47:13,831
Why won't you get a checkup? Why?

674
00:47:13,898 --> 00:47:16,400
The company's paying for it,
so why won't you go!

675
00:47:16,467 --> 00:47:18,602
What if you get cancer?

676
00:47:18,669 --> 00:47:20,071
What if you have rotten luck

677
00:47:20,137 --> 00:47:22,340
and hear you only have
six months left!

678
00:47:22,406 --> 00:47:24,942
Do whatever you want!

679
00:47:27,712 --> 00:47:29,513
Are you crazy?

680
00:47:29,580 --> 00:47:32,283
How dare you yell in the office!

681
00:47:32,350 --> 00:47:33,484
I'm sorry.

682
00:47:34,418 --> 00:47:35,586
I'm sorry.

683
00:47:47,665 --> 00:47:48,766
Hello?

684
00:47:49,667 --> 00:47:50,901
-How is it?
-What?

685
00:47:50,968 --> 00:47:53,571
Let's grow cabbages. Cabbages!

686
00:47:53,637 --> 00:47:56,474
Well? Mind-blowing, right?

687
00:47:58,042 --> 00:48:01,379
They pay a measly 1.5 million won
and treat you like dirt,

688
00:48:01,445 --> 00:48:04,215
so quit this lousy temp job

689
00:48:05,049 --> 00:48:06,984
and come with me.

690
00:48:13,357 --> 00:48:14,992
Get lost.

691
00:48:16,093 --> 00:48:17,895
Han-cheol, wait, wait, wait!

692
00:48:17,962 --> 00:48:19,296
Wait!

693
00:48:19,363 --> 00:48:23,267
If this works out,
we can drop an album. An album!

694
00:48:23,334 --> 00:48:27,037
So let's have a blast again
just like the old days.

695
00:48:27,104 --> 00:48:29,273
Come on, Han-cheol.

696
00:48:30,040 --> 00:48:31,242
-Huh?
-It's too late.

697
00:48:32,209 --> 00:48:35,179
Man, when you think it's too late,
it's the best time to start,

698
00:48:35,246 --> 00:48:36,781
as the wise old gem of a--

699
00:48:36,847 --> 00:48:38,449
It's too late, you bastard!

700
00:48:38,516 --> 00:48:41,719
You scared me! Just say no,
why are you making a scene?

701
00:48:41,786 --> 00:48:44,021
You're always like this. Always.

702
00:48:44,088 --> 00:48:46,157
You always keep a way out

703
00:48:46,223 --> 00:48:47,958
ready to bail if things go south.

704
00:48:48,025 --> 00:48:49,927
Even in the band, you cared more
about your studies,

705
00:48:49,994 --> 00:48:50,928
and now too.

706
00:48:51,695 --> 00:48:54,131
You've never once risked your life
and gone all in.

707
00:48:54,198 --> 00:48:55,833
Am I wrong?

708
00:49:03,574 --> 00:49:06,544
Hey, Han-cheol! Hey, hey!

709
00:49:06,610 --> 00:49:08,946
Hey, you cowardly bastard!

710
00:49:09,013 --> 00:49:11,482
Hey! Don't you come!

711
00:49:12,883 --> 00:49:14,985
SPARTAN PREP ACADEMY
STARTS SEPT 1

712
00:49:17,488 --> 00:49:20,157
You get what I mean, right?
Huh? What do you think?

713
00:49:21,225 --> 00:49:23,494
Eye-popping, right? Huh?

714
00:49:23,561 --> 00:49:25,896
Well, it sounds plausible for now.

715
00:49:25,963 --> 00:49:27,531
It somewhat makes sense too.

716
00:49:28,399 --> 00:49:29,867
Thing is…

717
00:49:29,934 --> 00:49:32,102
Say cabbage prices soared this year
like you said.

718
00:49:32,770 --> 00:49:34,104
That's the retail price.

719
00:49:34,171 --> 00:49:36,674
The farm-gate price
will be way lower than that.

720
00:49:37,308 --> 00:49:38,175
Sharp.

721
00:49:38,242 --> 00:49:41,011
That's the most crucial point!

722
00:49:41,078 --> 00:49:43,814
Why can't farmers make money?

723
00:49:43,881 --> 00:49:46,050
It's distribution. Distribution!

724
00:49:46,116 --> 00:49:49,653
Because middlemen skim off
too much of the margin.

725
00:49:49,720 --> 00:49:54,258
But if we can cut out
that middleman margin…

726
00:49:54,325 --> 00:49:56,126
How about that?

727
00:49:56,193 --> 00:49:57,428
How?

728
00:49:57,495 --> 00:49:58,696
We

729
00:49:58,762 --> 00:50:01,265
load up a truck, go to the city,
and sell them ourselves!

730
00:50:01,332 --> 00:50:05,569
Sell them 500 won cheaper than stores
and they'll sell like hotcakes.

731
00:50:05,636 --> 00:50:09,173
Well? You're totally falling for it,
right? Huh?

732
00:50:11,976 --> 00:50:14,078
Sounds plausible, but still…

733
00:50:14,144 --> 00:50:15,412
What, what, man!

734
00:50:15,479 --> 00:50:18,215
If it's this easy to make money,
why don't people

735
00:50:18,282 --> 00:50:19,950
want to farm?

736
00:50:22,152 --> 00:50:23,921
Well, that's obvious.

737
00:50:23,988 --> 00:50:25,756
Okay, first,

738
00:50:25,823 --> 00:50:28,859
they lack the vision
to read the future.

739
00:50:28,926 --> 00:50:31,829
Second, even if people think of it,

740
00:50:31,896 --> 00:50:34,164
it's hard to take action like me.

741
00:50:35,032 --> 00:50:36,700
That killed all my trust.

742
00:50:37,568 --> 00:50:39,436
This bastard is being
so damn picky.

743
00:50:39,503 --> 00:50:41,872
What'll you do if you pass
that petty civil service exam?

744
00:50:41,939 --> 00:50:44,408
Making a pittance of a salary,

745
00:50:44,475 --> 00:50:46,877
issuing resident copies
all day, every day?

746
00:50:46,944 --> 00:50:49,113
Cabbages at least have hope!

747
00:50:49,179 --> 00:50:51,448
Does your life have as much hope
as a cabbage worm, bastard!

748
00:50:51,515 --> 00:50:54,818
Why are you talking trash
first thing in the morning!

749
00:50:54,885 --> 00:50:56,687
And you think just anyone can farm?

750
00:50:56,754 --> 00:50:58,889
Cabbage is nothing, man.

751
00:50:58,956 --> 00:51:01,292
You plant seeds, water them,
and they shoot right up.

752
00:51:01,358 --> 00:51:03,193
When they grow, slice them right off.

753
00:51:03,260 --> 00:51:05,396
-Think I can't do that?
-Because I know you can't.

754
00:51:05,462 --> 00:51:06,964
Hey! Don't go!

755
00:51:07,798 --> 00:51:10,334
Don't go! If you guys don't go,
I'll go down alone!

756
00:51:10,401 --> 00:51:13,470
Instead of curling up
like a caterpillar

757
00:51:13,537 --> 00:51:15,639
in this hopeless pit of Seoul,

758
00:51:15,706 --> 00:51:18,042
even for a day, I'll live with a dream,
you bastard!

759
00:51:18,108 --> 00:51:19,743
Keep stuffing your face with MSG!

760
00:51:20,778 --> 00:51:23,013
Go on, step in dog crap on your way!

761
00:51:27,685 --> 00:51:29,119
They're all soggy.

762
00:51:30,521 --> 00:51:31,889
I'm really passing this.

763
00:51:45,836 --> 00:51:47,071
Cancer…

764
00:51:48,205 --> 00:51:49,640
Terminal.

765
00:51:50,374 --> 00:51:51,375
Why me?

766
00:51:52,343 --> 00:51:53,877
Why me of all people?

767
00:51:54,511 --> 00:51:58,515
I gave up everything I wanted
and did everything I was told, so why?

768
00:51:59,183 --> 00:52:01,218
Why me? Why, why?

769
00:52:01,285 --> 00:52:03,253
Why!

770
00:52:09,093 --> 00:52:10,327
I'm very sorry.

771
00:52:10,394 --> 00:52:12,029
-Pour both sides.
-Yes, I'm sorry.

772
00:52:12,096 --> 00:52:13,397
Have a seat.

773
00:52:14,865 --> 00:52:16,200
Hey, what are you doing?

774
00:52:16,266 --> 00:52:18,168
Stop that, come here,
and have a drink.

775
00:52:18,836 --> 00:52:20,270
Yes, Department Head, one moment, boss!

776
00:52:21,672 --> 00:52:23,073
Hey, intern.

777
00:52:23,140 --> 00:52:25,442
You ruined the mood,
so sing a song and hype it up.

778
00:52:25,509 --> 00:52:26,910
You were big in Hongdae?

779
00:52:26,977 --> 00:52:29,313
Huh? You were big in Hongdae?

780
00:52:29,380 --> 00:52:31,815
Let's see how good he really is!

781
00:52:31,882 --> 00:52:33,617
-Let's see.
-Sure, sure.

782
00:52:34,818 --> 00:52:36,353
What, you don't want to?

783
00:52:37,221 --> 00:52:38,555
Then don't.

784
00:52:38,622 --> 00:52:40,924
I already know how lousy a punk
like you is.

785
00:52:43,761 --> 00:52:45,129
Still, good for you,

786
00:52:45,195 --> 00:52:46,730
coming to your senses.

787
00:52:46,797 --> 00:52:50,000
Play in a band
and you're bound to starve to death.

788
00:52:50,067 --> 00:52:51,869
At best, you'd age out in Misari,

789
00:52:51,935 --> 00:52:53,303
strumming a guitar, right?

790
00:52:53,370 --> 00:52:56,273
He'd be lucky to strum a guitar
in Misari!

791
00:52:58,208 --> 00:53:00,411
You were just trying to look cool
in a band,

792
00:53:00,477 --> 00:53:01,945
so how could you get a job?

793
00:53:07,217 --> 00:53:08,452
I will do it.

794
00:53:09,553 --> 00:53:10,888
The song.

795
00:53:35,279 --> 00:53:37,247
Hey! Are you crazy?

796
00:53:39,183 --> 00:53:41,719
What? You told me to sing.

797
00:53:41,785 --> 00:53:43,921
Are you dying to get yourself killed?

798
00:53:43,987 --> 00:53:47,091
I'm not dying to get myself killed.

799
00:53:47,157 --> 00:53:50,894
I'm dying NOT to die, you bastard!

800
00:53:52,963 --> 00:53:54,698
Look at this punk!

801
00:53:54,765 --> 00:53:56,300
Your liver's swollen with nerve!

802
00:53:56,366 --> 00:53:58,168
How did you know

803
00:53:58,235 --> 00:53:59,803
my liver's swollen?

804
00:54:01,071 --> 00:54:02,773
My bad.

805
00:54:02,840 --> 00:54:05,976
Sorry a temp got a swollen liver,

806
00:54:06,643 --> 00:54:09,713
you high-and-mighty full-time bastard!

807
00:54:21,024 --> 00:54:22,760
Get out, get out!

808
00:54:44,448 --> 00:54:46,850
Whether it's a stairway to heaven

809
00:54:46,917 --> 00:54:49,987
or a stairway to hell, I don't know,

810
00:54:51,855 --> 00:54:53,557
but let's just go.

811
00:54:53,624 --> 00:54:55,025
Let's do this.

812
00:54:56,093 --> 00:54:57,227
You only live once.

813
00:55:01,632 --> 00:55:06,103
Those spineless, gutless,
disloyal jerks.

814
00:55:06,170 --> 00:55:09,039
If I ever see you guys again,
I'm not human.

815
00:55:09,106 --> 00:55:11,308
You pathetic losers, ptoo!

816
00:55:24,221 --> 00:55:25,856
What are you doing here?

817
00:55:29,259 --> 00:55:30,160
Let's go.

818
00:55:30,227 --> 00:55:32,429
Where? A hostess bar?

819
00:55:32,496 --> 00:55:34,364
To grow cabbages.

820
00:55:36,066 --> 00:55:38,202
What? Really? For real? Really?

821
00:55:38,268 --> 00:55:40,137
Hey!

822
00:55:41,538 --> 00:55:44,808
But if we don't drop an album,
you die by my hand.

823
00:55:44,875 --> 00:55:46,877
-Got it?
-Got it.

824
00:55:46,944 --> 00:55:48,979
Okay, I got it.

825
00:55:49,046 --> 00:55:52,482
I've already got a massive plan
all laid out!

826
00:55:52,549 --> 00:55:53,784
Don't worry.

827
00:55:53,851 --> 00:55:56,386
Come on, let's get some pork belly.

828
00:55:56,453 --> 00:55:57,988
Let's go.

829
00:55:59,189 --> 00:56:02,226
You've been making such great choices
lately.

830
00:56:02,292 --> 00:56:04,394
That's why I like you, Han-cheol.

831
00:56:04,928 --> 00:56:06,129
What's with this pigsty?

832
00:56:06,196 --> 00:56:07,364
What's that?

833
00:56:07,431 --> 00:56:09,233
Who's there?

834
00:56:11,869 --> 00:56:12,736
Ki-jun.

835
00:56:14,738 --> 00:56:15,839
Ki-jun?

836
00:56:20,611 --> 00:56:23,247
You? Don't tell me…

837
00:56:25,048 --> 00:56:27,784
On one condition.

838
00:56:28,385 --> 00:56:30,420
A condition?

839
00:56:30,487 --> 00:56:33,590
Tell me, just say the word!
I'll do anything for you!

840
00:56:33,657 --> 00:56:35,359
-What is it?
-Our…

841
00:56:37,461 --> 00:56:38,662
Let's change the band name.

842
00:56:38,729 --> 00:56:41,531
Seriously, let's not mess with EXO.

843
00:56:41,598 --> 00:56:43,734
You know what happens
if we mess with them.

844
00:56:43,800 --> 00:56:45,669
Shut up! Why change our name?

845
00:56:45,736 --> 00:56:47,070
They should!
We're the original!

846
00:56:47,137 --> 00:56:48,705
Suit yourself, then.

847
00:56:48,772 --> 00:56:51,108
Fine, Ki-jun, fine!

848
00:56:51,174 --> 00:56:53,310
I'm furious, pissed, and wronged,

849
00:56:53,377 --> 00:56:54,778
but I'll change it for you.

850
00:56:54,845 --> 00:56:56,546
Got it? Happy now?

851
00:56:56,613 --> 00:56:58,081
-Deal.
-Deal!

852
00:56:59,850 --> 00:57:00,817
All right!

853
00:57:00,884 --> 00:57:03,086
Hey, guys!

854
00:57:03,153 --> 00:57:05,255
Let's rock out again
just like the old days!

855
00:57:05,322 --> 00:57:08,358
Let's duke it out
with this lousy world!

856
00:57:09,359 --> 00:57:10,794
Let's go all the way.

857
00:57:10,861 --> 00:57:12,129
What's the worst that can happen?

858
00:57:12,896 --> 00:57:15,032
EXO-F, yeah!

859
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:25,642
-What is it?
-Look over there!

860
00:57:41,258 --> 00:57:42,592
HAN YU-NA! I'LL PROPOSE
WITH A 100-CARAT RING,

861
00:57:42,659 --> 00:57:44,261
SO DON'T CHEAT, WAIT!
FROM MK

862
00:57:44,928 --> 00:57:47,431
Yu-na, who's MK?

863
00:57:47,497 --> 00:57:49,066
You should do something like that.

864
00:57:49,132 --> 00:57:51,101
Give me a bit,
I'll go even bigger for you.

865
00:57:51,168 --> 00:57:52,436
Really?

866
00:57:59,743 --> 00:58:02,179
He's so hopeless.

867
00:58:16,360 --> 00:58:18,128
What's wrong with this…?

868
00:58:21,331 --> 00:58:24,634
That's broken. It never closes.

869
00:58:25,969 --> 00:58:27,204
Where have you been?

870
00:58:27,270 --> 00:58:29,106
I was sleeping
when new tenants' movers came in.

871
00:58:29,172 --> 00:58:30,707
Know how freaked out I was?

872
00:58:30,774 --> 00:58:34,244
Okay, sorry.
I had a quick stop to make.

873
00:58:34,311 --> 00:58:36,213
Forget it, forget it.

874
00:58:36,279 --> 00:58:38,148
If it's broken, fix it!

875
00:58:38,215 --> 00:58:39,583
What is this junk?

876
00:58:39,649 --> 00:58:41,985
Like I have money to fix it!

877
00:58:42,853 --> 00:58:44,821
Just be glad it even runs.

878
00:58:46,990 --> 00:58:49,159
-Where'd Han-cheol go?
-Don't know.

879
00:58:52,963 --> 00:58:54,531
Hey, by the way…

880
00:58:55,165 --> 00:58:56,366
This…

881
00:58:59,202 --> 00:59:02,372
Shouldn't we have told Hyeok too?

882
00:59:03,173 --> 00:59:06,943
To his royal highness
born with a gold spoon in his mouth,

883
00:59:07,010 --> 00:59:08,612
farming makes no sense.

884
00:59:08,678 --> 00:59:12,149
And even if that bastard wanted to go,
I don't want him!

885
00:59:14,885 --> 00:59:16,686
-Let go!
-You let go first!

886
00:59:16,753 --> 00:59:17,754
Let go!

887
00:59:17,821 --> 00:59:20,223
-Let go on three.
-Fine, okay.

888
00:59:20,290 --> 00:59:22,926
-One, two…
-One, two, three!

889
00:59:25,929 --> 00:59:27,497
Hey!

890
00:59:27,564 --> 00:59:29,266
You threw yourself at him, bitch!

891
00:59:29,332 --> 00:59:31,735
I was dating him first!

892
00:59:31,802 --> 00:59:35,405
Dr. Kang and I even kissed!

893
00:59:35,472 --> 00:59:38,075
I even went to a hotel with Dr. Kang!

894
00:59:38,141 --> 00:59:41,845
He wouldn't let me sleep all night,
he was so full of fight!

895
00:59:41,912 --> 00:59:44,514
You Attack on Titan bitch!

896
00:59:49,553 --> 00:59:54,558
Pull the hospital shutter down!

897
00:59:55,759 --> 00:59:58,829
Call the police! Call the police!

898
00:59:58,895 --> 01:00:01,298
-Hey!
-Stop it, please!

899
01:00:04,167 --> 01:00:05,068
WARD 11B

900
01:00:05,135 --> 01:00:06,303
Get up here.

901
01:00:08,271 --> 01:00:10,907
-Hello, Chief!
-Why, you little bastard…

902
01:00:10,974 --> 01:00:13,243
-Have you eaten yet?
-What? Eaten?

903
01:00:13,310 --> 01:00:15,145
You turned the hospital into a circus,

904
01:00:15,212 --> 01:00:16,847
and you ask that, you punk?

905
01:00:16,913 --> 01:00:19,349
We all work to make a living,
so we still have to eat.

906
01:00:19,416 --> 01:00:21,118
Come on, my treat.

907
01:00:21,184 --> 01:00:22,853
Why, this little bastard…

908
01:00:22,919 --> 01:00:24,688
Why don't you stop here?

909
01:00:24,754 --> 01:00:26,723
I could let you hit me a few times,

910
01:00:26,790 --> 01:00:28,959
but can you handle the fallout?

911
01:00:29,025 --> 01:00:30,660
I'm just worried about you.

912
01:00:36,133 --> 01:00:37,801
Wow, your temper really mellowed.

913
01:00:37,868 --> 01:00:41,338
Playing it safe since you're eyeing
the Head of Surgery spot?

914
01:00:46,042 --> 01:00:48,945
Everyone here seems confused,

915
01:00:50,347 --> 01:00:52,649
so truth is, my dad is the director.

916
01:00:52,716 --> 01:00:53,884
The top dog here.

917
01:00:53,950 --> 01:00:55,652
That's why this esteemed man

918
01:00:55,719 --> 01:00:57,654
grovels to an intern like me.

919
01:00:58,388 --> 01:00:59,456
Anyone still lost?

920
01:01:02,192 --> 01:01:05,028
Oh, that's my dad right there!
The top dog here.

921
01:01:05,095 --> 01:01:06,730
Dad!

922
01:01:15,071 --> 01:01:17,207
Man, what a buzzkill.

923
01:01:21,711 --> 01:01:24,214
MEDICATION GUIDE
PATIENT: YOO HAN-CHEOL

924
01:01:42,332 --> 01:01:43,934
Buddy!

925
01:01:45,702 --> 01:01:47,537
Get off. I'm busy.

926
01:01:49,005 --> 01:01:51,241
Acting all busy, you punk. Going where?

927
01:01:51,308 --> 01:01:52,909
None of your business.

928
01:01:52,976 --> 01:01:55,745
Come on, where are you going?

929
01:01:55,812 --> 01:01:58,848
I was told never to tell you,
no matter what.

930
01:01:58,915 --> 01:02:00,183
What?

931
01:02:00,250 --> 01:02:01,484
Who?

932
01:02:01,551 --> 01:02:04,821
What wise guy on earth told you that…

933
01:02:05,889 --> 01:02:07,691
Must be Min-gi.

934
01:02:08,525 --> 01:02:09,759
What? Cabbage farming?

935
01:02:09,826 --> 01:02:11,628
Happy now? See ya.

936
01:02:14,898 --> 01:02:16,099
Cabbage farming…

937
01:02:18,068 --> 01:02:19,669
That sounds like fun.

938
01:02:22,739 --> 01:02:23,607
HANKOOK HOSPITAL

939
01:02:23,673 --> 01:02:25,008
Take me with you, buddy!

940
01:02:25,075 --> 01:02:26,743
Hey, you said you wouldn't come!

941
01:02:26,810 --> 01:02:29,145
You even swore on your father's name!

942
01:02:30,614 --> 01:02:32,682
-What do we do?
-Why did you let go?

943
01:02:32,749 --> 01:02:34,784
Just grab it! Grab it!
